Apply .claude/rules/code-quality.md § Comments to this project's src/main code: Javadoc is the only comment. Do it in two steps. First, convert every // and /* */ comment in src/main that is not one of the two exceptions. A reason that must survive the next edit goes into the Javadoc of the type or method it explains. A comment that only describes the code is replaced by a better name, or by an extracted method whose name says what the comment said. A TODO becomes an issue. List each file and what you plan for its comments, and wait for my go-ahead before you change anything. Second, add these modules to config/checkstyle/checkstyle.xml, exactly as written. At Checker level, before the TreeWalker: <module name="RegexpMultiline"><property name="id" value="LineComment"/><property name="fileExtensions" value="java"/><property name="format" value="^(?:(?&lt;!\{[ 	]{0,40}?
)|(?=[^
]*?
(?![ 	]*\})))[ 	]*//(?![ 	]*(?:NOSONAR|CHECKSTYLE:(?:OFF|ON)|spotless:(?:off|on)|@formatter:(?:off|on)) )"/><property name="message" value="code-quality.md § Comments: Javadoc is the only comment."/></module> <module name="RegexpMultiline"><property name="id" value="BlockComment"/><property name="fileExtensions" value="java"/><property name="format" value="^[ 	]*/\*(?!\*)"/><property name="message" value="code-quality.md § Comments: Javadoc is the only comment."/></module>. Inside the TreeWalker, replacing the existing TodoComment module: <module name="TrailingComment"><property name="format" value="^\s*$"/><property name="legalComment" value="^\s*(NOSONAR|CHECKSTYLE:(OFF|ON)|spotless:(off|on)|@formatter:(off|on)) "/></module> <module name="InvalidJavadocPosition"/> <module name="TodoComment"><property name="format" value=" TODO "/></module>. Change no behavior, and run ./mvnw verify.
